    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8b372743_72d98e5d",
        "filename": "src/ports/BUILD.bazel",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 348,
      "author": {
        "id": 6155
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-05T11:44:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In short: To overcome the cyclic dependency problem. \n\n`fontations_ffi:fontations_ffi` (the cc library) depends on `fontations:path_bridge_include` (i.e. the headers that allow Rust to call back to C++). As the latter has `#include \"SkPath.h:` in it, it won\u0027t compile without adding `skia_internal` or `skia_public` as a dependency. But then that creates a cyclic dependency (adding `skia_internal` to this `skia_cc_deps` here).\n\nSo we make the compilation of the path bridge code (headers to call back from Rust to C++) part of the filegroup and build it as part of the Skia C++ side things, and we depend only on the Rust side things here.",
      "parentUuid": "644398ea_f5b63df2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 348,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 348,
        "endChar": 50
      },
      "revId": "29ce031378698eaabdba76fc7048ebd508614b61",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
